Phase 5 — correctly support ZERO available fighters

This is critical.

Simply setting #0001.available = false is not enough because several current flows assume a fighter can always be instantiated.

Audit every route that selects, defaults, loads, or starts a fighter.

js/core/app.js

The app already calculates:

CHARACTERS.find((c) => c.available)?.id ?? null

With every fighter disabled/removed, the initial Quick Battle and Watch selections should therefore be null.

Preserve that null-safe behavior.

Also preserve the rule that only available fighters are preloaded. With zero available fighters, startup must not preload #0001 as playable content.

Do not replace null with '0001'.

Do not introduce a fallback that selects the first definition regardless of available.

js/screens/battle-screen.js

The current battle setup obtains definitions through getCharacter(...) and then assumes they are valid.

Add or strengthen validation so a battle cannot start with:

* a missing fighter ID
* null
